      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-224971",
      ":question/problem": "Let $f$ and $g$ be Boolean functions of two variables defined as\n$f(x_{1}, x_{2}) = x_{1} \\cdot x_{2}, g(x_{1}, x_{2}) = (x_{2} + 1)mod2$.\nComplete the following table corresponding to the function $g(x_{1}, f(x_{1}, x_{2}))$.\n\n| $x_{1}$ | $x_{2}$ | $g(x_{1}, f(x_{1}, x_{2}))$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $0$ | $0$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $0$ | $1$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $1$ | $0$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $1$ | $1$ | {{field-4}} |\n\nHint: If $x$ is an integer, then\n$xmod2 = {0,\\begin{vmatrix}ifxis even, \\\\ 1,\\end{vmatrix}ifxis odd$."
